</h3><ul><li>24 Oreo-style chocolate sandwich cookies</li><li>5 tbsp melted butter</li><li>1 pint chocolate frozen custard, softened 10 minutes</li><li>1 pint vanilla frozen custard, softened 10 minutes</li><li>3/4 cup hot fudge sauce, divided</li><li>6 chocolate sandwich cookies, roughly crushed for topping</li><li>Whipped cream, optional</li></ul></div><div><h3>Step-by-step</h3><ol><li>Crush 24 cookies finely and mix with melted butter.</li><li>Press firmly into a 9-inch pie plate across the bottom and up the sides. Freeze 15 minutes.</li><li>Spread chocolate frozen custard into the crust in an even layer. Freeze 20 minutes.</li><li>Warm about 1/2 cup hot fudge only until spreadable—not hot. Spread over the chocolate layer and freeze another 15 minutes.</li><li>Spread vanilla frozen custard on top. Sprinkle with crushed cookies.</li><li>Freeze at least 4 hours, preferably overnight.</li><li>Let stand at room temperature 8–12 minutes before slicing. Serve with remaining fudge and whipped cream if wanted.</li></ol></div></div><div class="note"><strong>KaySo note:</strong> Dip your knife in hot water and wipe it dry between cuts for clean slices.</div><div class="recipe-actions"><button data-share-recipe>↗ Share Recipe</button><button data-copy-recipe>Copy Recipe</button><span class="status"></span></div></div></details><details class="recipe" id="grasshopper-pie" data-title="Grasshopper Pie"><summary><span class="recipe-title">Grasshopper Pie</span><span class="open-label">Open Recipe ↓</span></summary><div class="recipe-body"><div class="meta"><div><span>Serves</span>6</div><div><span>Total Time</span>30 minutes + chilling</div><div><span>Difficulty</span>Easy–Moderate</div><div><span>Equipment</span>9-inch pie plate; mixer.</div></div><div class="makeahead"><strong>Make-ahead:</strong> Best made the day before.</div><div class="cols"><div><h3>Ingredients